# Trivy ignore file — Phase 1 BETA documented exceptions
#
# Per .claude/rules/release-deploy-standard.md §3.1 PRE-RELEASE:
#   "Trivy zero HIGH/CRITICAL recommended không mandatory cho *-staging.* tags"
#
# Per Trivy best practice (https://trivy.dev/docs/v0.70/configuration/filtering/):
#   - Each entry has explicit rationale + expiry + tracking gap
#   - NO blanket suppression — each CVE evaluated individually
#   - Re-evaluate at expiry; bump dep OR re-document
#
# All 6 entries below = Java JAR transitive deps from Spring Boot 3.5.14.
# Tracking gap: GAP-440 (Spring Boot dep bump 3.5.14 → latest 3.5.x — fixes
# Tomcat + Jackson; Tika + Commons BeanUtils need explicit dep override).
#
# Phase 1 BETA risk acceptance: invite-only ~10-20 tenants, network-isolated
# ALB ingress, no public crawler/scanner exposure for the patch window.

# === Tomcat embed (Spring Boot transitive, ETA fix Spring Boot 3.5.16+) ===
# CVE-2026-34483: Information disclosure due to improper encoding
# Affects: org.apache.tomcat.embed:tomcat-embed-core 10.1.53
# Fix: Tomcat 10.1.55+ (Spring Boot bump pulls in)
# Risk acceptance: BETA invite-only; no path-traversal exploit applicable
# Expiry: 2026-06-07 (30 days)
CVE-2026-34483

# CVE-2026-34486: Missing Encryption of Sensitive Data
# Affects: org.apache.tomcat.embed:tomcat-embed-core 10.1.53
# Fix: Tomcat 10.1.55+
# Risk acceptance: TLS terminated at ALB; in-cluster traffic isolated
# Expiry: 2026-06-07
CVE-2026-34486

# CVE-2026-34487: Information disclosure via sensitive data in log file
# Affects: org.apache.tomcat.embed:tomcat-embed-core 10.1.53
# Fix: Tomcat 10.1.55+
# Risk acceptance: BETA log access restricted to ops; no log-mining surface
# Expiry: 2026-06-07
CVE-2026-34487

# === Jackson Core (Spring Boot transitive, ETA fix Spring Boot 3.5.16+) ===
# GHSA-72hv-8253-57qq: Number Length Constraint Bypass in Async Parser
# Affects: com.fasterxml.jackson.core:jackson-core 2.19.4
# Fix: jackson-core 2.20+
# Risk acceptance: BETA invite-only; no untrusted JSON ingestion (all FE
# traffic via gateway with size limits per kitehub.gateway routes config)
# Expiry: 2026-06-07
GHSA-72hv-8253-57qq

# === Apache Tika (kitehub-platform document parser) ===
# CVE-2025-66516: tika-parser-pdf-module CRITICAL
# Affects: org.apache.tika:tika-core 2.9.2
# Fix: tika 2.9.4 OR 3.0.0 (kitehub-platform pom.xml needs explicit override)
# Risk acceptance: BETA tika usage = AI Branding logo metadata only; no
# untrusted PDF upload from public surface (admin-only consent flow per
# ai-branding-guidelines.md §2.5 input cap)
# Expiry: 2026-06-07
CVE-2025-66516

# === Apache Commons BeanUtils ===
# CVE-2025-48734: PropertyUtilsBean does not suppress class-property access
# Affects: commons-beanutils:commons-beanutils 1.9.4
# Fix: commons-beanutils 1.10.0+ (transitive — likely from spring-data or
# velocity dep; needs explicit pin)
# Risk acceptance: BETA invite-only; bean property access constrained by
# Spring Boot strict deserialization defaults
# Expiry: 2026-06-07
CVE-2025-48734

# === Alpine OS base image (gnutls — affects all 10 service images) ===
# CVE-2026-33845: gnutls vulnerability CRITICAL
# Affects: alpine 3.23 base image (all Java + Node services share this base)
# Fix: alpine 3.24+ (eclipse-temurin:*-jre-alpine + node:*-alpine bump)
# Risk acceptance: BETA invite-only; TLS terminated at ALB (gnutls in-image
# only used for outbound TLS to AWS APIs which validates certs server-side);
# in-cluster mTLS bypass not exposed
# Expiry: 2026-06-07
# Tracked: GAP-442 alpine 3.23 → 3.24 base image bump (10 Dockerfiles)
CVE-2026-33845

# === Notes ===
# 5 warning-severity CVEs (CVE-2024-25710, CVE-2024-26308, CVE-2025-31672,
# CVE-2025-48924, CVE-2026-34500) are MEDIUM/LOW — not fail-gating.
# CVE-2026-33846 + CVE-2026-3833 (gnutls HIGH) — covered by CRITICAL-only
# staging gate (release-deploy-standard.md §3.1); production v1.0.0+ tag
# requires alpine bump to clear (GAP-442).
#
# Re-evaluate this file at expiry 2026-06-07. Spring Boot bump (GAP-440) +
# alpine bump (GAP-442) expected to clear 6 of 7 entries automatically.

# === GAP-456 Group C — npm internals bundled in Node base image ===
# These 4 CVEs live in `usr/local/lib/node_modules/npm/node_modules/...` —
# i.e. inside the npm bundled with the Node base image used at BUILD time
# only. They are NOT application dependencies (no `package.json` import,
# no FE bundle inclusion, no runtime exposure). Reachability ~0.
# Fix path: rebase to fresher node:*-trixie tag when next CVE wave hits;
# defer until then per release-fix-retry-budget.md (don't churn base image
# for non-reachable CVEs).
# Reviewer: @nguyenvankiet (solo-dev acting Security Lead, 2026-05-09).
# Expiry: 2026-08-09 (re-evaluate at quarter end).

# CVE-2026-33671: picomatch (npm bundled regex util)
CVE-2026-33671

# CVE-2026-33672: picomatch (second advisory, same package)
CVE-2026-33672

# CVE-2026-33750: brace-expansion (npm bundled glob expansion)
CVE-2026-33750

